    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Will Guzzardi has represented the 39th District in the Illinois House since January 2015. He is an Assistant Majority Leader, Democratic Caucus co-budgeteer, Illinois House Progressive Caucus co-chair, and Economic Opportunity and Equity committee chair. Before taking office, he was a Huffington Post Chicago editor and a University of Chicago admissions writer. His campaign says he passed 2019 legislation raising the state's minimum wage to $15 by 2025. He was the House sponsor of a bill limiting out-of-pocket insulin costs to $100 for state-regulated plans. In 2021, he introduced a bill to repeal the state rent-control ban so municipalities could cap rents. He sponsored a 2025 Prisoner Review Board reform to give victims more participation.",
